rk  Phoenix's box office bombings spurred  Disney brass to rework its priorities at  Marvel Studios evidently wanted Feige to  focus on rebuilding the x-men brand a  source close to variety indicated that  Walt Disney Studios co-chairman Alan  Bergman insisted on an end to the Sony  talks after Dark Phoenix blocked though  it's tempting to jump on the x-men  killed spider-man train fans should take  this report with a grain of salt no one  but the parties involved in the Disney  Sony split know what really happened and  plenty of rumors have surfaced in the  time since the  News broke some claim that Disney and  Sony are secretly working things out  behind the scenes while others are  convinced that what's done is done and  there's no turning back at this point in  time it's anyone's guess what's coming  next  even with Feige and spider-man actor Tom  Holland having recently addressed the  situation during the 2019 d23 Expo in  late August the men spoke with  Entertainment Weekly about the studio's  breakup and Spidey's MCU exit howl and  express gratitude for getting to play  spider-man for what he called five  amazing years with the character while  buggies stated that the deal between  Disney and Sony was quote never meant to  last forever my parents are dead it's  interesting to consider Dark Phoenix in  the future of the x-men franchise being  a major force behind Disney's decision  to walk away from the negotiating table  and let Sony regain sole ownership over  spider-man Holland's web slinging hero  has proven wildly successful for both  studios with many fans and critics  agreeing that his iteration of  spider-man is the best one yet the most  recent franchise entry  spider-man far from home earned over a  billion dollars worldwide becomes Sony's  top earning movie ever one could argue  that it makes little sense that Disney  and Marvel would prioritize fixing a  broken franchise over keeping a really  good thing going either way if the  studio's really have split it's hard not  to be worried about the fate of that  third Tom Hollands star in spider-man  movie well at least we can all agree  that third one's always the worst  however it doesn't seem totally  unreasonable that by game company would  want to end the ongoing tug of war with  Sony / spider-man and instead focus  their time and expertise on building the  x-men film series back up the spider-man  movies clearly aren't hurting for  attention in any aspect and thanks to  pikeys inputs are on the steadiest  ground they've been on since Sam Raimi's  original trilogy it seems that the  biggest takeaway from all the Spidey  related news is this Sony will probably  be fine Disney and Marvel will probably  be fine and both studios will hopefully  be able to coexist in peace College  spider-man isn't going anywhere in the  immediate future and neither are the  fans of the franchise for now at least  check out one of our newest videos right  here Plus even more looper videos about  spider-man are coming soon subscribe to  our YouTube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

